title: ActOneNotes
act: Arrival
style: note
---
Act I, one day. The courier arrives with three letters. Brandt has the key and Maud the oil: the lamp must burn before the night, or the ship of Act II strikes the rocks. The dues and the cat are deeds that the vote of Act III remembers. #line:0a9fe37
===

title: Events
act: Arrival
scenario: The dark lamp
quest: letters
when: once
when: $act == Act.Arrival
---
The causeway to Brinemoor is open at low tide. You cross it with the post bag on your back. #line:033f504
Three letters for the island: one for the harbourmaster, one for a fisher called Maud, one for Odile, who keeps the light. #line:020005d
The lighthouse stands dark over the town. #line:06d6ed6
<<give letter 3>>
<<set $quest_letters = QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed letters>>
===

title: LettersLeft
act: All
quest: letters
---
// Said after each letter is handed over
<<if item_count("letter") > 0>>
    You have [plural value={item_count("letter")} one="one letter" other="% letters" /] left in the bag. #line:049ffa0
<<else>>
    The bag is empty. Every letter found its hands. #line:039eb4b
    <<set $quest_letters = QuestState.Succeeded>>
    <<quest_changed letters>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Brandt
act: All
quest: letters
when: not $letter_brandt
---
<<take letter>>
<<set $letter_brandt = true>>
Brandt: From the bank. They never write to say thank you. #line:0695abb
<<detour LettersLeft>>
===

title: Brandt
act: Arrival
scenario: The dark lamp
quest: lamp
when: $act == Act.Arrival
when: $quest_lamp == QuestState.Active and not has_item("key") and not $lamp_lit
---
Brandt: The keeper has been gone three days, and the lamp with her. She left me the spare key. #line:058d769
-> I will light the lamp. Give me the key. #line:06d1280
    Brandt: Take it. And bring it back. #line:0540aea
    <<give key>>
-> It is not my lamp. #line:00e9487
    Brandt: It will be everyone's, tonight. #line:0d70b7a
    -> Then give me the key. #line:brandt_key_after_all
        Brandt: Take it. And bring it back. #line:brandt_key_given_after_all
        <<give key>>
    -> Good day. #line:brandt_key_refused
===

title: Brandt
act: Arrival
scenario: The harbour dues
when: $act == Act.Arrival
when: $dues_asked and not $dues_settled
---
Brandt: Joss sent you? The dues are {$dues} shillings a boat now. The harbour has debts. #line:0d7121b
-> Twelve is too much. The boats cannot pay it. #line:0793d5b
    // Eleven at most, less with luck
    <<set $dues = round(11 - dice(6) / 2)>>
    <<set $dues_cut = true>>
    Brandt: You are worse than the bank. [pause=600 /]{$dues}, then. #mood:angry #line:0f244fd
    Brandt: Half before midsummer: {format("{0:0.0}", $dues / 2)} shillings a boat, and not a day late. #line:0b402c7
-> It is your harbour. #line:0d4253e
    Brandt: It is. Good day. #line:07ebff8
<<set $dues_settled = true>>
===

title: Brandt
act: All
when: always
---
<<if $act == Act.Arrival>>
    Brandt: Post goes in the box. Boats pay at the desk. #line:0e69836
<<elseif $act == Act.Wreck>>
    Brandt: The cargo is counted. Every crate. #line:0fa1983
<<else>>
    Brandt: The bell rings at nightfall. Then we will see. #line:02a62d4
<<endif>>
Brandt: Mind the tide. #line:mind_the_tide
===

title: Maud
act: All
quest: letters
when: not $letter_maud
---
<<take letter>>
<<set $letter_maud = true>>
Maud: My sister. Every spring she asks me to leave the island. Every spring I mend the nets. #line:01696c0
<<detour LettersLeft>>
===

title: Maud
act: Arrival
scenario: The dark lamp
quest: lamp
when: $act == Act.Arrival
when: $quest_lamp == QuestState.Active and not $oil_allowed
---
Maud: Odile never let that lamp go dry. Something is wrong up there. #line:052df87
Maud: A lamp needs oil. Take a can from my shed, by the pier. #line:06c56f0
<<set $oil_allowed = true>>
===

title: Maud
act: All
when: always
---
=> Maud: The fish don't wait, courier. #line:0e7e4a4
=> Maud: Mind the nets. They cost more than the boat. #line:0dd1149
=> Maud: Odile used to wave from up there. Every evening. <<if not $odile_here>> #line:021102c
=> Maud: Look at that. Somebody in the lamp room again. <<if $odile_here>> #line:031db8b
===

title: Joss
act: Arrival
scenario: The harbour dues
when: $act == Act.Arrival and not $dues_asked
---
Joss: Twelve shillings a boat! It was eight at Candlemas. #mood:angry #line:0239596
Joss: Brandt will not hear it from us. But the post walks into that office every day. #line:0a30e6a
-> I will speak to him. #line:0dea67d
    Joss: Do that, and I owe you a fish. #line:08424c1
-> I only carry letters. #line:0a0b72e
    Joss: Then carry this one: twelve is too much. #line:08dab30
<<set $dues_asked = true>>
===

title: Joss
act: All
when: always
---
<<if $dues_cut>>
    <<once>>
        Joss: {$dues} shillings! You got him down. Nobody gets him down. #mood:glad #line:0159224
    <<endonce>>
<<endif>>
Joss: What can I do for the post? #line:04ef25c
// With nothing left to ask, the options are passed over
-> Have you a fish to spare? It is for a cat. <<if $quest_cat == QuestState.Active and not has_item("fish") and not $cat_down>> #line:048bf45
    Joss: For Biscuit? Take a herring. That cat eats better than I do. #line:0b68f89
    <<give fish>>
-> How is the catch? <<if not visited("JossCatch")>> #line:06ed0dd
    <<detour JossCatch>>
Joss: Back to the nets, then. #line:040c64d
===

title: JossCatch
act: All
---
Joss: Herring, mostly. And a sea boot, once. I threw it back. #line:0d05338
===

title: Pim
act: All
quest: cat
when: $quest_cat == QuestState.NotStarted
---
Pim: Biscuit went up the roof of the inn and he won't come down. He's been there since breakfast. #mood:sad #line:022a326
-> I will get him down. #line:0653a38
    <<set $quest_cat = QuestState.Active>>
    Pim: He likes herring. Joss has herring. #line:0c0f5a6
-> I have letters to carry. #line:0db9361
    <<set $quest_cat = QuestState.Offered>>
    Pim: He'll still be there. He's stubborn. #line:0491787
<<quest_changed cat>>
===

title: Pim
act: All
quest: cat
when: $quest_cat == QuestState.Offered
---
Pim: Did you change your mind? About Biscuit? #line:04da65d
-> Yes. I will get him down. #line:04c10a5
    <<set $quest_cat = QuestState.Active>>
    <<quest_changed cat>>
    Pim: Herring! He likes herring. Joss has some. #line:0fa9bc7
-> Not yet. #line:068587b
    Pim: All right. #line:0c14fe5
===

title: Pim
act: All
when: always
---
<<if $cat_down>>
    => Pim: Biscuit says thank you. He says it by sitting on your bag. #mood:glad #line:0f1a2ba
    => Pim: He only went up there to look at the sea, I think. #line:09d75c7
<<elseif $quest_cat == QuestState.Active>>
    Pim: Herring. Joss has herring. #line:0a72a20
<<else>>
    => Pim: Gran says the lamp is the island's eye. #line:02769d5
    => Pim: I can count every boat from here. Do you want to hear? #line:0e66da4
<<endif>>
===

title: Cat
act: All
quest: cat
when: $quest_cat == QuestState.Active and has_item("fish")
---
<<take fish>>
You hold up the herring. [pause=700 /]The cat thinks about it. [pause=700 /]Then it walks down the drainpipe as if it had meant to all along. #line:0794d95
<<walk Pim Cat>>
Pim: Biscuit! #mood:glad #line:0f68b14
<<set $cat_down = true>>
<<set $quest_cat = QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed cat>>
===

title: Cat
act: All
quest: cat
when: not $cat_down
---
<<once>>
    A ginger cat looks down at you from the roof of the inn. It is not coming down. #line:09ddecf
<<else>>
    The cat blinks. Still not coming down. #line:0cf5206
<<endonce>>
===

title: Tam
act: All
when: always
---
Tam: [select value={time_of_day()} morning="Morning" afternoon="Afternoon" evening="Evening" night="Late" /], courier. The Anchor is open. #line:0613ee5
-> What is cooking? #line:0a27db2
    <<detour InnMenu>>
-> Nothing, thank you. #line:0308330
Tam: Mind the step. #line:0646de0
===

title: InnMenu
act: All
---
<<if visited("InnMenu")>>
    Tam: You again? Still stew. You have asked [plural value={visited_count("InnMenu")} one="once" other="% times" /] already. #line:0fa2ec0
<<else>>
    Tam: Stew. It is always stew. With fish in it, when Joss is lucky. #line:022c9d9
<<endif>>
===

title: OilCan
act: Arrival
quest: lamp
when: $oil_allowed and not $oil_taken
---
You take a can of lamp oil from Maud's shed. #line:09cd9a8
<<give oil>>
<<set $oil_taken = true>>
===

title: OilCan
act: Arrival
quest: lamp
when: not $oil_allowed and not $oil_taken
---
Cans of lamp oil, in somebody's shed. Not yours to take. #line:05566b4
===

title: LighthouseDoor
act: Arrival
scenario: The dark lamp
quest: lamp
when: $act == Act.Arrival and $quest_lamp == QuestState.NotStarted
---
You knock. Nobody answers. Odile's letter stays in the bag. #line:09fa220
High above, the lamp room is dark. Night will come, and ships with it. #line:0253eee
<<set $quest_lamp = QuestState.Active>>
<<quest_changed lamp>>
===

title: LighthouseDoor
act: Arrival
scenario: The dark lamp
quest: lamp
when: $quest_lamp == QuestState.Active and $lamp_can_be_lit
---
The key turns. You climb the stair, fill the lamp and light it. #line:0007cf9
<<take oil>>
<<set $lamp_lit = true>>
<<set $quest_lamp = QuestState.Succeeded>>
<<quest_changed lamp>>
The beam swings out over the water. #line:0462f0b
===

title: LighthouseDoor
act: Arrival
scenario: The dark lamp
quest: lamp
when: $quest_lamp == QuestState.Active and not $lamp_can_be_lit
---
<<if has_item("key")>>
    The key fits. But the lamp is dry: it needs oil. #line:0a27745
<<elseif has_item("oil")>>
    You have oil, and a locked door. #line:025a73b
<<else>>
    Locked. Someone on the island must have a spare key. #line:0b046a4
<<endif>>
===

title: Bell
act: Arrival
when: $act == Act.Arrival
---
The town bell. Ring it without a reason and Brandt will find you one. #line:00f2eca
===

title: Events
act: Arrival
scenario: The dark lamp
when: $act == Act.Arrival
when: $is_night
when: $lamp_lit
---
Night. The lamp turns over Brinemoor, and far out a ship turns with it. #line:01ec186
She finds the channel and drops anchor in the bay. #line:033a916
<<set $ship_anchored = true>>
<<jump ActTwo>>
===

title: Events
act: Arrival
scenario: The dark lamp
quest: lamp
when: $act == Act.Arrival
when: $is_night
when: not $lamp_lit
---
Night falls on a dark lamp. #line:0d3b30f
Far out, a ship looks for the channel and finds the rocks. #line:0b0d4a9
<<set $wreck_aground = true>>
<<set $quest_lamp = QuestState.Failed>>
<<quest_changed lamp>>
<<jump ActTwo>>
===
